licensed separately under AGPL-3.0-or-later.
Source and license: https://github.com/pgsty/silo/tree/RELEASE.2026-10-18T00-00-00Z
Other Compose services retain their upstream licenses and sources.
The Redis 8 container uses the upstream AGPLv3 licensing option. Original
Redis notices and the AGPL license are retained under deploy/redis/ and
in that container's license directory. Source: https://github.com/redis/redis
Milvus 3.0.3 (Apache-2.0) and NSQ 1.3.0 (MIT) have their Go products rebuilt
using the pinned source and independent dependency locks in deploy/.
Their containers retain original Go/dependency licenses under
/usr/share/licenses/milvus-rebuild/ and /usr/share/licenses/nsq/ respectively.
etcd 3.5.33 (Apache-2.0), which stores Milvus metadata, is rebuilt from its
pinned source with upstream's own dependency lock; its container retains the
etcd, Go and dependency licenses under /usr/share/licenses/etcd/.

The media container builds separate FFmpeg 9.0.2 tools with libx264
under GPL-2.0-or-later, and libwebp 1.6.0 tools under their BSD-style license.
Their original licenses, exact corresponding source archives, build inputs
and configuration are included in /opt/media/licenses/ and /opt/media/source/;
see deploy/media/NOTICE.txt. These tools are not relicensed under Apache-2.0.

